{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the Rephaim.</b> This is what is written, \"the land of Rephaim is reckoned\" (Deuteronomy 3:13). And do not wonder because \"the Canaanite and the Jebusite\" are written after it. Know that the seven nations are all Canaanites, and Canaan had eleven sons, and after the six are mentioned, he says \"the Canaanite\" for the remainder. And likewise in this passage they are ten in detail, and elsewhere in general; and similarly, \"Judah and Israel were many\" (1 Kings 4:20), even though Judah is of Israel."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:44.931760525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}